%% title: Life of a wave opened by the daemon
%% desc: From the sensor to Excel delivery, including preflight, repair and verify.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant SE as sensor
  participant WF as wave_flow (DBOS)
  participant AR as article_run.py
  participant RN as runner (agy)
  participant DB as monocle.db
  participant DL as write_user_output
  SE->>WF: trigger T1, T2 or T3 is met and an L1 mandate exists
  WF->>WF: preflight: breaker, disk, DB write access, prefix
  WF->>AR: prepare (the smaller of wave.limit and max_limit)
  AR->>AR: select articles, split into batches of 50, write packets
  AR->>RN: analyze, batches run in parallel
  RN-->>AR: article-compact-v2 for each batch
  loop at most 2 rounds
    AR->>RN: repair the missing part
    RN-->>AR: additional records
  end
  AR->>AR: finish: expand, validate, matcher
  AR->>DB: ingest through DoD
  AR->>AR: verify coverage of at least 90% in both layers
  alt pass
    WF->>DL: deliver xlsx (best effort)
    WF-->>SE: DONE
  else fail
    WF-->>SE: PARKED, waiting for a rerun
  end
